0.6 "Derivative Work" means any work that is based on, derived from, or
    incorporates the Software or any part of it.

0.7 "Substantially Similar Work" means the Software or a Derivative Work
    whose functional core remains the functional core of the Software.
    A work is presumed Substantially Similar if any of the following
    applies:
    (a) a majority of its source files are identical or substantially
        identical to source files of the Software;
    (b) its externally visible feature set and behavior substantially
        reproduce those of the Software;
    (c) modifications are limited to renaming, rebranding, reformatting,
        or changes to a minority of files.
    Renaming or repackaging never removes Substantial Similarity.

0.8 "Patch" means a machine-readable difference description (for example
    a unified diff) that (a) refers to the Software at the Canonical
    Source, (b) does not contain the complete Software or a Substantially
    Similar Work, and (c) is intended to be applied to an unmodified copy
    of the Software obtained from the Canonical Source.

0.9 "Publish" or "Redistribute" means making a work available to any
    third party, in source or binary form, by any means — including but
    not limited to public or private repository hosting, package
    registries, download servers, mirrors, or physical media — whether
    or not for a fee, and whether under the name "go-quality-authority" or
    any other name. Providing the Software solely to employees,
    contractors, or agents of Your organization for internal Use is not
    Publishing.

